-- =============================================================
-- COMPONENT: Filter chips ("HTML slicer") - cross-filtering chip row
-- Layer:     shell - page furniture (header/menu/chips); native text/buttons/navigators exist but cannot carry this styling and live values.
-- Binding:   Values  = [HTML Chip]
--            Context = Sales[Category]      (or any column to filter by)
-- Edition:   Regular + Secure
-- Status:    doc-based (HTML Content 2.0), NOT run in Power BI
-- REQUIRED:  Format pane > Cross-filtering > Enable = On.
--            Without it the chips are display-only.
-- What this is: cross-filter selection (like clicking bars in a chart).
-- What it is NOT: a real slicer. No select-all, no search, no single-select
-- mode, no slicer sync. Multi-select on desktop via Ctrl+click; custom
-- visuals do not support multi-select in the mobile apps.
-- Selected state: unselected entries get class 'unselected' (default dim
-- 70%, configurable). There is no 'selected' class; style the rest state.
-- Template:  Row template = {{row}}
-- =============================================================

HTML Chip =
VAR CatName = SELECTEDVALUE ( Sales[Category] )
RETURN
    "<span class='chip' dir='rtl' lang='he'>" & CatName & "</span>"

